###### 3.2 *Average Velocity* $aV := \bar{v}_{[t_0,t_1]}$ over the Time Interval $[t_0,t_1]$
###### 3.2.1 Definition of $aV := \bar{v}_{[t_0,t_1]}$
(cf. Walck, 2022, p.36)

*Velocity is defined to be the rate at which position changes. The 'average velocity' over the time interval that starts at time $t_0$ and ends at time $t_1$ is* (Walck, 2022, p.36):

$\bar{v}_{[t_0,t_1]} = \frac{\Delta_{position}}{\Delta_{time}} = \frac{x(t_1)-x(t_0)}{t_1-t_0}\;\;\text{(4.1)}$

where

$\Delta{position} := x(t_1)-x(t_0)\;\; = change \text{ in position}$
$\Delta{time} := x(t_1)-x(t_0)\;\; = change \text{ in time}$

"

