###### 3.10 Introducing Derivatives
(cf. Walck, 2022, p.38f)

###### 3.10.1 Definitions

###### Instantaneous Velocity

$v(t) = \lim_{\Delta t\to 0} \frac{x(t+\Delta t/2)-x(t-\Delta t/2)}{\Delta t}\;\;\;\text{ (4.3)}$

$\;$

###### Derivative with Operator $D$

$D(t) = \lim_{\epsilon\to 0} \frac{x(t+\epsilon)-x(t-\epsilon)}{\epsilon}\;\;\;\text{ (4.4)}$

$\;$

###### Function Equation: Velocity = Derivative of Position Function $x(t)$

$v = Dx\;\;\;\text{ (4.5.1)}$
$D: x \rightarrow v\;\;\;\text{ (4.5.2)}$

$\forall t: v(t) = Dx(t)\;\;\;\text{ (4.6.1)}$
$D: \forall t: x(t) \rightarrow v(t)\;\;\;\text{ (4.6.2)}$

$\forall t: v(t) = \frac{dx(t)}{dt}\;\;\;\text{ (4.7)}$

"

