###### 3.10 Higher Order Function: *Numerical* Derivatives in Julia
(cf. Walck, 2022, p.40)

###### 3.10.1 Definition of Function $derivative$
*A derivative takes a function as input and gives a function as output. In other words, a derivative is a function from functions to functions. A function that takes another function as input or returns a function as output is called a 'higher-order function'.* (cf. Walck, 2022, p.40f)

The *numeric* variant of a *derivative* is defined over a *small* intervall $\epsilon$. So the type contains a $\epsilon \in ΔTime$ in the domain.

$Derivative = PositionFunction \times Time \times ΔTime \rightarrow Velocity$
$\epsilon \in ΔTime := Time$
$D: (t \mapsto l, t, l) \mapsto v$
$derivative: (t \mapsto l, t, l) \mapsto v$
"

# ╔═╡ efacc19f-5368-43da-b2ba-f7d917736dff
md"
---
###### 3.10.2 Code of $derivative$
"

# ╔═╡ e1904090-2b8f-44c1-9769-b5dab6ab6f29
ϵ = 1E-6

# ╔═╡ d83c9fef-12f9-44b2-bc98-70a2ce6ee8cf
md"
###### 1st Method of Function $D$ (= untyped)
"

# ╔═╡ 08b10adf-619f-4210-94d8-dd685b28f895
derivative(x, t; dt = ϵ) = 
	(x(t + dt/2) - x(t - dt/2))/dt

# ╔═╡ affed044-d5e7-4c5e-9cea-f94e3cef028a
md"
###### 2nd Method of Function $D$ (= typed)
"

# ╔═╡ 3e479fba-ddb0-4b07-9361-a662e0a7ffa2
derivative(x::PositionFunction, t::Time; dt::ΔTime = ϵ)::Velocity = 
	(x(t + dt/2) - x(t - dt/2))/dt

# ╔═╡ 402378b5-085e-4d38-a95d-185790f84e91
md"
###### 3rd Method of Function $D$ (= typed) with $f$ as *Array of Values*
Derivative of Function $f$ as Set of Values $fs = \{f(t)| t_{min} \le t_{max}\}$
"

# ╔═╡ 247d4d9c-f244-4a16-8b7b-fdd6d6233773
findfirst(isequal(3.1), [1.1, 3.1, 4.3])

# ╔═╡ 11e0f231-938a-486c-8971-43a4e3f0c4c3
function derivative(xs::Vector{Float64}, t::Time, ts::Vector{Float64})
	tInt = findfirst(isequal(t), ts)::Int
	if tInt-1 == 0
		(xs[tInt+1] - xs[tInt])/(ts[tInt+1] - ts[tInt])
	elseif tInt+1 > length(xs)
		(xs[tInt] - xs[tInt-1])/(ts[tInt] - ts[tInt-1])
	else
		(xs[tInt+1] - xs[tInt-1])/(ts[tInt+1] - ts[tInt-1])
	end # if
end # function derivative

# ╔═╡ c06fd220-784b-4d2b-a8ce-4ce504b7262d
methods(derivative)

