###### 3.12 Modeling the *Simple Harmonic Oscillator (SHO)*: Position, Velocity, and Acceleration
(cf. Walck, 2022, p.41f)

Walck's object of study is a highly idealized *car* with *one-dimensional* position function $x(t) = cos\ t.$ Instead we prefer to study an *one-dimensional harmonic oscillator* with the same position function. This model comes into *technical* existence as a *mass-spring* or as a [*scotch-yoke-system*](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotch_yoke).
