###### 3.12.4 Integration of *Velocity* under Constraints
(cf. Walck, 2022, p.43)

- for *constant* velocity $v(t)=v_0=const$:

$\int_{t_0}^t v(t) dt = \int_{t_0}^t Dx(t) dt$

$\int_{t_0}^t Dx(t) dt = \int_{t_0}^t v_0 dt = x(t)-x(t_0)$

- and for *linear ascending* or *descending* $v(t) = v_0t$:

$\int_{t_0}^t Dx(t) dt = \int_{t_0}^t v_0t dt = x(t)-x(t_0)=v_0t-x(t_0)$

$PositionConstVelocity := Position \times Velocity \times Time \rightarrow Position$
$positionConstVelocity: (x_0, v_0, t) \mapsto x_t$

"

# ╔═╡ 8031993a-ce9e-41a2-aba8-844da08b2f99
positionConstVelocity(x0, v0, t) = v0*t + x0

# ╔═╡ 24f40603-0cc0-4a7a-8f53-f82ef2df26b5
positionConstVelocity(x0::Position, v0::Velocity; t::Time=0.0) = v0*t + x0

