##### 4. Summary
One-dimensional motions are reified in the [*Simple Harmonic Oscillator (SHO)*](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simple_harmonic_motion). Physical systems operating as *SHOs* are *mass-spring* or [*Scotch Yoke Systems SYS*](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotch_yoke). 

The *amplitude* of *characteric* variables $x_{Op}, v_{Op}$, and $a_{Op}$ can be plotted in a common diagram. $a_{Op}$ was obtained in double ways. One, as a *first-order derivative* of $Dv_{Op}$ and one as a *derivative of second-order* $D^2 x_{Op}$

We could easily replace Haskell function by Julia's. The main differenc is that Haskell's are *currified* and Julia's usually *not*. This has consequences for type definitions. If you want *currified* versions in Julia you have to explicity code them as *higher-order* functions. 
"

